Package: influ2
Title: Model-Neutral Influence Diagnostics for Fisheries CPUE Models
Version: 1.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person(given = "Darcy", family = "Webber",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           email = "darcy.webber@quantifish.co.nz"),
    person(given = "Nokome", family = "Bentley",
           role = c("ctb", "cph"),
           comment = "Original influence methodology and legacy validation implementation"),
    person(given = "Trophia Ltd", role = "cph",
           comment = "Legacy validation implementation")
    )
Description: Calculates and visualises how changes in the distribution of
    explanatory variables affect standardised catch-per-unit-effort indices.
    A model-neutral S3 diagnostic provides consistent summaries and plots for
    frequentist, Bayesian, mixed-effect, spatial, and spatiotemporal models.
    Posterior and joint-simulation calculations are reduced directly to
    compact diagnostic estimands to avoid retaining observation-by-draw
    arrays. The influence definitions follow Bentley et al. (2012)
    <doi:10.1093/icesjms/fsr174>.
